{"status":"ok","message-type":"work-list","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"facets":{},"total-results":863813,"items":[{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,23]],"date-time":"2026-10-23T10:59:22Z","timestamp":1792753162644,"version":"4.5.0"},"reference-count":23,"publisher":"AIP Publishing","issue":"4","content-domain":{"domain":["pubs.aip.org"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2007,4,1]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>A type of superhydrophobic surface consists of a solid plane boundary with an array of grooves which, due to the effect of surface tension, prevent a complete wetting of the wall. The effect is greatest when the grooves are aligned with the flow. The pressure difference between the liquid and the gas in the grooves causes a curvature of the liquid surface resisted by surface tension. The effects of this surface deformation are studied in this paper. The corrections to the effective slip length produced by the curvature are analyzed theoretically and a comparison with available data and related mathematical models is presented.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1063\/1.2716438","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2007,4,24]],"date-time":"2007-04-24T17:51:56Z","timestamp":1177437116000},"update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1063\/aip-crossmark-policy-page","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":216,"title":["A note on the effective slip properties for microchannel flows with ultrahydrophobic surfaces"],"prefix":"10.1063","volume":"19","author":[{"given":"M.","family":"Sbragaglia","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"University of Twente Faculty of Applied Sciences, IMPACT, and Burgerscentrum, , AE 7500 Enschede, The Netherlands"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"A.","family":"Prosperetti","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"University of Twente Faculty of Applied Sciences, IMPACT, and Burgerscentrum, , AE 7500 Enschede, The Netherlands and Department of Mechanical Engineering