66"}],"container-title":["Physics of Fluids"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/pubs.aip.org\/aip\/pof\/article-pdf\/doi\/10.1063\/1.2716438\/14850957\/043603_1_online.pdf","content-type":"application\/pdf","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"syndication"},{"URL":"https:\/\/pubs.aip.org\/aip\/pof\/article-pdf\/doi\/10.1063\/1.2716438\/14850957\/043603_1_online.pdf","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2023,6,29]],"date-time":"2023-06-29T00:45:24Z","timestamp":1687999524000},"score":72.68086,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/pubs.aip.org\/pof\/article\/19\/4\/043603\/256116\/A-note-on-the-effective-slip-properties-for"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2007,4,1]]},"references-count":23,"journal-issue":{"issue":"4","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2007,4,1]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1063\/1.2716438","ISSN":["1070-6631","1089-7666"],"issn-type":[{"value":"1070-6631","type":"print"},{"value":"1089-7666","type":"electronic"}],"published-other":{"date-parts":[[2007,4]]},"published":{"date-parts":[[2007,4,1]]},"article-number":"043603"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,6]],"date-time":"2026-10-06T09:22:20Z","timestamp":1791278540554,"version":"4.1.0"},"reference-count":42,"publisher":"Cambridge University Press (CUP)","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2007,4,26]],"date-time":"2007-04-26T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1177545600000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/www.cambridge.org\/core\/terms"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["J. Fluid Mech."],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2007,5,10]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>This paper studies the nature of the effective velocity boundary condition for liquid flow over a plane boundary on which small free-slip islands are randomly distributed. It is found that an effective Navier partial-slip condition for the velocity emerges from a statistical analysis valid for arbitrary fractional area coverage \u03b2. As an example, the general theory is applied to the low-\u03b2 limit and this result is extended heuristically to finite \u03b2 with a resulting slip length proportional to<jats:italic>a<\/jats:italic>\u03b2\/(1 \u2212 \u03b2), where<jats:italic>a<\/jats:italic>is a characteristic size of the islands. A specification of the nature of the free-slip islands is not required in the analysis. They could be nano-bubbles, as suggested by recent experiments, or hydrophobic surface patches. The results are also relevant for ultra-hydrophobic surfaces exploiting the so-called \u2018lotus effect\u2019.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1017\/s0022112007005149","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2007,4,26]],"date-time":"2007-04-26T11:00:06Z","timestamp":1177585206000},"page":"435-451","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":77,"title":["Effective velocity boundary condition at a mixed slip surface"],"prefix":"10.1017","volume":"578","author":[{"given":"M.","family":"SBRAGAGLIA","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"A.","family":"PROSPERETTI","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"56","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2007,4,26]]},"reference":[{"key":"S0022112007005149_N105F3","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1121\/1.1908834"},{"key":"S0022112007005149_N102E5","volume-title":"Microhydrodynamics","author":"Kim","year":"1991"},{"key":"S0022112007005149_N10255","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1021\/la000219r"},{"key":"S0022112007005149_N1068D","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/sia.2079"},{"key":"S0022112007005149_N101C9","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1063\/1.858104"},{"key":"S0022112007005149_N106CE","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevLett.87.096105"},{"key":"S0022112007005149_N10543","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.102